  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "sensitivity-intro",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Financial Assumptions\n",
    "\n",
    "We introduce revenue and operating assumptions to evaluate project feasibility:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Average Monthly Rent per Unit\n",
    "- Retail Rent per SF\n",
    "- Operating Expense Ratio\n",
    "- Development Cost (from prior section)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "assumptions",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Base Assumptions\n",
    "units = 265\n",
    "avg_monthly_rent = 2650  # $ per unit\n",
    "retail_sf = 50000\n",
    "retail_rent_psf = 35  # annual $/SF\n",
    "opex_ratio = 0.30\n",
    "\n",
    "total_hard_cost = 54444486.46\n",
    "\n",
    "# Annual Revenue Calculations\n",
    "residential_revenue = units * avg_monthly_rent * 12\n",
    "retail_revenue = retail_sf * retail_rent_psf\n",
    "\n",
    "gross_revenue = residential_revenue + retail_revenue\n",
    "noi = gross_revenue * (1 - opex_ratio)\n",
    "\n",
    "gross_revenue, noi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "yield-metrics",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Yield Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "We evaluate basic return using a simplified yield-on-cost metric."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "yield",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Yield on Cost\n",
    "yield_on_cost = noi / total_hard_cost\n",
    "yield_on_cost"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "sensitivity-section",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sensitivity Analysis: Rent vs. Cost\n",
    "\n",
    "This analysis tests how changes in residential rent and construction costs impact yield.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Rent range: ±20%\n",
    "- Cost range: ±20%"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "sensitivity",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sensitivity ranges\n",
    "rent_range = np.linspace(0.8, 1.2, 5) * avg_monthly_rent\n",
    "cost_range = np.linspace(0.8, 1.2, 5) * total_hard_cost\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create sensitivity table\n",
    "sensitivity_matrix = pd.DataFrame(index=[round(r,0) for r in rent_range],\n",
    "                                  columns=[round(c/1e6,1) for c in cost_range])\n",
    "\n",
    "for r in rent_range:\n",
    "    for c in cost_range:\n",
    "        res_rev = units * r * 12\n",
    "        total_rev = res_rev + retail_revenue\n",
    "        noi = total_rev * (1 - opex_ratio)\n",
    "        yoc = noi / c\n",
    "        sensitivity_matrix.loc[round(r,0), round(c/1e6,1)] = round(yoc, 4)\n",
    "\n",
    "sensitivity_matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "interpretation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Rows represent changes in **average monthly rent**\n",
    "- Columns represent **total development cost (in $ millions)**\n",
    "- Values represent **yield on cost (NOI / Cost)**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Insights:\n",
    "- Higher rents significantly improve returns due to operating leverage\n",
    "- Cost overruns compress yield quickly\n",
    "- The project’s feasibility is highly sensitive to achieving projected rents\n",
    "\n",
    "This framework can be extended further with financing, cap rates, and IRR modeling."
   ]
  }
